### Summary

The refactor to read boots before the helpers exist is sound. The new Boot ordering matches the new test, which would fail on the old code. There are two non-blocking points: `EnsureReady` now runs a `simctl` call inline with no deadline of its own, and `TestHubStartRecordsEverySimulatorsBoot` no longer tests the `EnsureReady` wiring.

<details><summary>What the change connects to (2 closed, 0 open)</summary>

Questions the reviewer answered about what this change does to the running product. The engine checked that the cited lines exist, not that the answers are true.

**Closed, with the lines they rest on**
- Boot reads simctl boots before the stream helper is created and stores that value once Boot finishes (replaces recordBoots after Boot) (`backend/internal/adapters/device/local/provider.go:1010`) — A simulator rebooted outside AO right after AO's helper was made is now detected on the next lease look, and the hub is restarted so touch input works again. If it fails: If simctl fails, currentBoots returns nil, helperBoot is empty and nothing is recorded. The next look is then a first sighting, so one outside reboot can go unnoticed, which matches the old behaviour… Evidence: `backend/internal/adapters/device/local/provider.go:1010-1015`, `backend/internal/adapters/device/local/provider.go:1040-1044`, `backend/internal/adapters/device/local/provider.go:1097-1119`, `backend/internal/adapters/device/local/provider.go:695-735`.
- EnsureReady reads boots synchronously before startHub and stores them under p.mu after p.hub is set (`backend/internal/adapters/device/local/provider.go:241`) — The first device operation is delayed by one simctl call. If NoteBooted recorded a newer boot while the hub was starting, the older pre-start read overwrites it. The result is at most one extra hub restart, which the comment accepts. If it fails: A hung simctl blocks EnsureReady for every caller until ctx ends. See the finding on provider.go:241. Evidence: `backend/internal/adapters/device/local/provider.go:192-194`, `backend/internal/adapters/device/local/provider.go:237-257`, `backend/internal/adapters/device/local/provider.go:126-128`.

